    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is already possible to the extent which this module is designed. It intentionally can operate only based on cursor neighborhood (two characters to its left and right). It is not (and won't be) able to condition action based on anything else.\r\n\r\nHere is the config which will insert only `(` \\ `[` \\ `{` if the next character is `)` \\ `]` \\ `}`:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.pairs').setup({\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    ['('] = { action = 'open', pair = '()', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\][^%)]' },\r\n    ['['] = { action = 'open', pair = '[]', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\][^%]]' },\r\n    ['{'] = { action = 'open', pair = '{}', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\][^%}]' },\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2022-11-22T07:56:03Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/164#issuecomment-1323253494",
